# React 19 Patterns

## 1. Components

- **Arrow functions + `FunctionComponent` type** — no `FC` (alias), no function declarations.
- **Type**: `interface Props { ... }` — always explicit. No inline anonymous types for props.
- **Output contract**: the `FunctionComponent<Props>` variable annotation declares the output; where it is absent, use an explicit `(): ReactElement` return type — enforced by `@typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type` (inline callbacks exempt).
- **Ref**: In React 19, refs are passed as **regular props**. **NEW or touched code: ALWAYS ref-as-prop, NEVER `forwardRef`.** `forwardRef` is deprecated but still functional (not removed) — the ONLY sanctioned usage is the legacy `src/components/layout/Main` shell; leave it as-is, do NOT migrate it and do NOT introduce `forwardRef` anywhere else.
- **Named exports only**: Default exports only for lazy-loaded pages (React Router lazy).

```typescript
import type { FunctionComponent } from 'react';

// React 19 — no forwardRef needed, ref as regular prop
interface InputProps extends React.InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLInputElement> {
    label?: string;
    ref?: React.Ref<HTMLInputElement>;
}

export const Input: FunctionComponent<InputProps> = ({ label, ref, ...props }) => {
    return (
        <label>
            {label && <span>{label}</span>}
            <input ref={ref} {...props} />
        </label>
    );
};
```

## 2. Component Architecture: Logic Separation

- **Components must be maximally presentational** — UI only.
- **Extract runtime orchestration to a local hook** next to the component: `useComponentName.ts`.
- **Extract pure deterministic computation to utilities** (`src/lib/` or local utility file).
- **Mixed logic rule**: split pure computation out first; keep the hook as a thin orchestration layer.
- Component imports hook: `import { useComponentName } from './useComponentName'`.
- **Folder ladder (this template, flat — not FSD):** `src/components/{ui,common,layout}` → `hocs/` → `hooks/<domain>/` → `pages/<Page>/` (with its page-local `use<Page>.ts`) → `router/`; `lib/` and `store/<domain>/` sit beneath the UI layers and never import `components` or `pages` (`import-x/no-restricted-paths` in `eslint.config.js`).

```
UserCard/
  UserCard.tsx          # UI only, imports useUserCard
  useUserCard.ts        # All logic, state, event handlers
  UserCard.test.tsx     # Integration test
```

## 3. Hooks

- **Arrow functions** for hooks.
- **Explicit return type**: hooks declare their output (`(): UseXResult`) — enforced by `@typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type`.
- **Domain grouping**: `src/hooks/<domain>/hookName.ts` + `hookName.test.ts` alongside.
- **Direct imports** — no `index.ts` barrel re-exports.
- **Rules of Hooks**: Hooks only in React components or other hooks. Never in callbacks, loops, or conditions.

```typescript
// Bad — hook in callback
const handleClick = (): void => { const data = useQuery(...); };

// Good — hook at top level
const { data } = useUserQuery(id);
const handleClick = (): void => doSomethingWith(data);
```

## 4. Pages

```
// Entry page (no lazy) — direct named export
export const HomePage: FunctionComponent = () => { ... };

// All other pages (lazy-loaded)
// PageName.tsx — component
export const NotFoundPage: FunctionComponent = () => { ... };

// index.ts — lazy wrapper
import { lazy } from 'react';
export const NotFoundPage = lazy(() => import('./NotFoundPage'));

// Router — always wrap lazy pages with WithSuspense
{ path: '*', element: WithSuspense(<NotFoundPage />) }
```

## 5. HOCs

- HOCs in `src/hocs/`.
- `WithSuspense` wraps all lazy-loaded components in the router.
- Function call style (not decorator): `WithSuspense(<Component />)`.

## 6. Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML first: `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`.
- Add ARIA only where semantic HTML is insufficient.
- Loading states: `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"`.
- Critical errors: `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"`.
- Forms: `<label>` always associated with input (via `htmlFor` or wrapping).

## 7. Anti-Patterns (FORBIDDEN)

- ❌ `React.forwardRef` in NEW or touched code — deprecated in React 19; ALWAYS pass `ref` as a regular prop. Narrow legacy carve-out: `src/components/layout/Main` only — leave as-is, never replicate the pattern in new files.
- ❌ `FC` from react — use `FunctionComponent` explicitly (ESLint enforced).
- ❌ Function declarations for components — use `const X: FunctionComponent<Props> = () => {}`.
- ❌ Arrow function components with default exports (confuses lazy imports).
- ❌ Logic > 10 lines directly in JSX — extract to hook.
- ❌ `import React from 'react'` — not needed in React 19 with JSX transform.
- ❌ `any` in component props.

## 8. Interaction & base-layer states (binding)

- **States must be PERCEPTIBLY DISTINCT, not merely present.** A hover / active / focus / selection colour must not resolve to ≈ the element's own default or background colour — verify it is VISIBLE. Failure modes seen in the wild: a base link colour equal to its `hover:` colour (zero visible hover — only the cursor changes); a `::selection` highlight built on a near-background token (invisible selection). Chrome/nav links default to a neutral (`text-muted-foreground`) so the `hover:text-primary` shift shows.
- **Compound states must stay COHERENT.** When two states co-occur (focus+invalid, hover+selected, disabled+focus) they must not visually fight — the more urgent state owns the shared channel (e.g. an invalid field recolours its focus ring, `aria-invalid:focus-visible:ring-destructive`, so focused+invalid reads as one error state; disabled cancels hover). Check state PAIRS, not just singles.
- **Base-layer globals** (`::selection`, base links, `:focus-visible`) must be perceptibly distinct AND must NOT be built on quiet near-background tokens (`--muted`, or an `--accent` that is a slate-3-style near-background neutral). System feedback (selection, focus ring) is built on `--primary` / `--ring`, never the quiet hover token. If you define `::selection`, use `background-color: hsl(var(--primary)); color: hsl(var(--primary-foreground));` — a quiet token renders the highlight invisible.

## 9. Composition over props

- **Trigger**: a component is about to gain a third boolean prop, or a second variant axis next to its `cva` variants. Stop adding props.
- **Prefer slots**: `children`, named slot props (`icon`, `footer`), or `asChild` render delegation via `@radix-ui/react-slot` — the shadcn `Button` in `src/components/ui/button.tsx` already does this.
- **Or a compound component**: the parent owns state in a context, sub-components read it (`Panel` / `Panel.Header` / `Panel.Body`).
- A new prop is right only when it changes the component's own behaviour, not what it renders.

```tsx
// Before: <Panel title="…" showIcon iconLeft compact />  — every combination is a branch inside Panel
// After: the caller composes what the panel renders (sketch, not a shipped component)
<Panel>
    <Panel.Header icon={<Star />}>{title}</Panel.Header>
    <Panel.Body>{children}</Panel.Body>
</Panel>
```
